{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund improved aftercare, support & advice for mothers after caesarean sections",
        "additional_details": "In our view, post-caesarean aftercare urgently needs improvement. We call for standardised scar care, abdominal rehabilitation, pelvic health and mental-health support. We believe this should be basic care following major abdominal surgery. With caesareans accounting for around 45% of UK births and increasing, we call on aftercare to evolve. \u201cRest and don\u2019t lift anything heavy\u201d is not enough now. Mothers deserve consistent, evidence-based support and properly trained professionals to improve recovery and outcomes.",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to fund improved post-caesarean aftercare across the NHS including standardised scar-care, abdominal rehabilitation, pelvic health & mental-health support. With caesareans accounting for around 45% of births (& increasing) mothers require consistent, specialist aftercare",
